      {
        "id": 1217188,
        "name": "Rebecca Chran",
        "username": "Rebecca_Chran",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/rebecca_chran/{size}/174594_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-12-11T06:31:58.673Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’ve been crawling through all the EVE related data and I came upon this dev blog from way back:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox whitelistedgeneric\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.eveonline.com/article/building-a-balanced-universe\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"04:19PM - 03 December 2013\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">EVE Online – 3 Dec 13</a>\n  </header>\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:600/388;\"><img src=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/original/3X/8/b/8b3a181a4510ddc661ff97f9fa7a846bd66b1d35.png\" class=\"thumbnail\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.eveonline.com/article/building-a-balanced-universe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Building a Balanced Universe | EVE Online</a></h3>\n\n<p>Building a Balanced Universe Hello everybody, my name is CCP Prism X and I am a Libra! This summer we saw a welcome influx of players with the release of EVE Online: Odyssey. On occasions as such we usually celebrate our great success by pulling out...</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>I noticed this is a problem ideally suited for some ML tinkering (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simulated_annealing\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simulated_annealing</a> + some clustering algorithm for example). Have any of you devs implemented anything along those lines yet or does this sound like a good approach?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "posts_count": 4,
        "updated_at": "2019-12-11T06:32:59.853Z",
